    {
      "finding_id": "S-1",
      "decision": "severity-calibrated",
      "source_file": "src/sqllens/tools/query_database.py",
      "claim_text": "No test covers handing the conversation turn to a queued waiter after the holding call is cancelled. Every cancellation test either cancels a call with no waiter parked behind it or cancels the waiter instead of the holder, so the entry.lock.release() in _conversation_turn's finally block is never exercised with someone waiting on it. A regression that dropped or moved that release would leave the next call on the same conversation id blocked until its client times out while the suite still passes.",
      "original_severity": "important",
      "calibrated_severity": "suggestion",
      "evidence": "Over-grade gate: shapes 1 and 3 both matched. Shape 3 — raised by one agent only (corroboration 1), prflow:pr-test-analyzer, an empirical over-grader named in the shape, with no other shadow finding and neither shadow checklist FAIL covering this defect. Shape 1 — the suite catches the named regression RED: there is exactly one entry.lock.release() in the module (query_database.py:191, in _conversation_turn's finally), shared by the normal and cancel paths, and tests/unit/test_query_database_queue.py::test_same_conversation_id_runs_one_at_a_time requires it to fire, asserting agent.entered reaches two entries only after the first call completes. Dropping or moving that release therefore fails an existing test RED, contrary to the finding's premise that the suite would still pass. Fail direction: none on shipped code; the release is present and correct, and checklist items VC-62 and VC-63 passed. The uncovered case is narrower than stated: only a future change adding a cancel-specific path that bypasses the shared finally would escape, and no such path exists today. Blast radius: a narrow future-regression class causing a hang on the next same-conversation call; no present defect and no fail-open on any current input. Consistency: the same run graded three structurally identical test-coverage gaps at Suggestion, including the shadow's own S-2 and S-3 and the primary engine's row-cap gap in iterations 1 and 3, so Important is the outlier grade here. Calibrated to suggestion, which triggers no promotion; the gap is real and is listed as an unresolved shadow note for follow-up."
    }
  ],
